[TITLE]
SNET - Simple network to illustrate the water-energy (pump) nexus
One reservoir, one pump, one demand junction, one storage tank.
Pump duty-cycles on tank level + diurnal demand -> a clean, nonzero
mean pump load (~19.5 kW) for the nexus electrical coupling.

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elev   Demand   Pattern
 N1   0      0                     ;pump discharge node
 N2   0      25       DEM          ;demand node (25 LPS average)

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID   Head   Pattern
 R1   0                            ;source at ground level

[TANKS]
;ID   Elev   InitLvl  MinLvl  MaxLvl  Diam   MinVol  VolCurve
 T1   25     3        0       6       12     0                ;elevated storage

[PIPES]
;ID   Node1  Node2  Length  Diam   Rough  MinorLoss  Status
 P1   N1     N2     500     300    130    0          Open  ;pump -> demand
 P2   N2     T1     100     400    130    0          Open  ;demand <-> tank

[PUMPS]
;ID   Node1  Node2  Parameters
 PU1  R1     N1     HEAD C1        ;lift from reservoir to N1

[CURVES]
;ID   X(flow LPS)  Y(head m)
 C1   50           40             ;single design point -> EPANET builds the curve

[PATTERNS]
;ID   Multipliers (24 hourly values, diurnal demand)
 DEM  0.5  0.4  0.4  0.5  0.7  1.0  1.4  1.6  1.5  1.3  1.2  1.1
 DEM  1.0  1.0  1.1  1.2  1.4  1.6  1.5  1.3  1.0  0.8  0.6  0.5

[CONTROLS]
 LINK PU1 OPEN  IF NODE T1 BELOW 1.5
 LINK PU1 CLOSED IF NODE T1 ABOVE 5.5

[TIMES]
 Duration            24:00
 Hydraulic Timestep  1:00
 Pattern Timestep    1:00
 Report Timestep     1:00
 Pattern Start       0:00
 Report Start        0:00
 Start ClockTime     12 am
 Statistic           NONE

[OPTIONS]
 Units               LPS
 Headloss            H-W
 Specific Gravity    1.0
 Viscosity           1.0
 Trials              40
 Accuracy            0.001
 Unbalanced          Continue 10
 Pattern             1
 Demand Multiplier   1.0
 Tolerance           0.01

[COORDINATES]
;Node  X      Y
 R1    0      50
 N1    10     50
 N2    30     50
 T1    30     80

[END]
